  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nAn upper ridge and Bermuda high pressure will be centered off \nthe coast through Saturday with mainly isolated shower and\nthunderstorm chances during the afternoon, mainly along the sea\nbreeze. The ridge becomes suppressed late in the weekend as \nshortwave energy pushes across the mid-Atlantic with more of a \nzonal pattern developing next week with a series of shortwave \ntroughs pushing across the area. Precip chances will be near \nclimo each day with scattered showers and thunderstorms \ndeveloping each afternoon, then dissipating with loss of heating\nduring the evening. The severe threat appears minimal through \nthe period with limited shear. \n\nA gradual warming trend will continue into next week as well \nwith highs in the lower 90s inland through the weekend, then \nwarming in to the mid 90s next week. Temps generally in the mid \nto upper 80s along the coast. The probabilities for Major Heat \nRisk increase to around 60-80% Monday through Thursday of next \nweek.",
